# Accepted, justified findings -- not hidden, just not blocking. Worked
# example of the trivyignore-path mechanism: each entry below was checked
# individually against the CVE's own "Fixed Version" field at the date
# noted. See docs/quality-gates.md for why this repo's own ci.yml also
# runs container-scan as soft-fail on top of this list -- Trivy's live
# vulnerability DB surfaced a shifting superset of OS-package findings
# across consecutive runs the same day, too volatile for a small ignore
# list alone to track reliably. This file stays as the reference example
# for consumers whose base image has a smaller, more stable finding set.

# zlib1g 1:1.2.13.dfsg-1 -- CRITICAL, no fix version published (checked
# 2026-08-27). demo-app never decompresses untrusted zlib-compressed data;
# the package is present only as a base-image transitive dependency.
CVE-2023-45853

# libsqlite3-0 3.40.1-2+deb12u2 -- CRITICAL, no fix version published
# (checked 2026-08-27). demo-app has no database and never invokes sqlite3.
CVE-2025-7458

# util-linux-extra 2.38.1-5+deb12u3 -- HIGH, no fix version published
# (checked 2026-08-27). demo-app's container runs as a non-root user and
# never invokes any util-linux binary; these are base-image utilities the
# application itself has no code path that reaches.
CVE-2026-53615
CVE-2026-53613
